==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{proto|Germanic|gǣ-, gai-|lang=ang}}.  The verb was defective in Germanic and may only have existed in the present tense.  Cognate with Old Saxon {{term|-gan|lang=osx}} (Dutch {{term|gaan|lang=nl}}), Old High German {{term|gan|lang=goh}} (German {{term|gehen|lang=de}}), Old Norse {{term|gá|lang=non}} (Swedish {{term|gå|lang=sv}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ɡɑːn/|lang=ang}}

===Verb===
{{ang-verb|head=gān}}

# to [[go]]

